## Goal
Make the lock timeout test in `internal/rulesfile/lock_unix_test.go` reliable (DEV-50) by removing its dependence on elapsed wall-clock time.

## Problems
None. The session slice contained no work for this repository. The wall-clock assertion is a timing check that can fail on slow or loaded machines, which is presumably what prompted the change.

## Decision
`TestLockTimesOutAgainstForeignHolder` no longer measures how long `Lock` waits, and the 150ms–1s window check is gone. The test now relies on the error text ("held by another writer") to show the lock timed out because a foreign holder had it. The follow-up check that `Lock` succeeds once the holder releases the flock is unchanged. Timing bounds are flaky under CI load, while the error message already shows that the timeout path ran.

